    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Beyond the bustling pilgrimage routes of Uttarakhand lies a tranquil Himalayan town where snow-clad peaks rise above ancient temples, sacred rivers flow through deep valleys, and spirituality is woven into everyday life. Welcome to Uttarkashi , a destination where nature, adventure, and devotion come together in perfect harmony.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Nestled along the banks of the mighty Bhagirathi River , Uttarkashi is often regarded as the spiritual counterpart of Kashi in the Himalayas. Surrounded by dense forests, alpine meadows, and towering mountain ranges, the town serves as a gateway to some of the region's most revered shrines, glaciers, and trekking routes. Whether it is the resonance of temple bells, the thrill of high-altitude trails, or the serenity of the Himalayan landscape, Uttarkashi offers an experience that is both rejuvenating and unforgettable.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The spiritual heart of Uttarkashi beats through its ancient temples and sacred sites. The revered Kashi Vishwanath Temple , dedicated to Lord Shiva, has drawn pilgrims for centuries and remains one of the town's most significant landmarks. Nearby, the ancient Shakti Temple stands as a symbol of faith and devotion, attracting visitors seeking blessings amidst the tranquil surroundings.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Beyond its religious significance, Uttarkashi is deeply connected to the traditions and culture of the Garhwal Himalayas. Local festivals, age-old customs, and warm community life reflect a heritage that has remained rooted in the mountains for generations.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Uttarkashi is where the Himalayas reveal their most captivating beauty. Verdant valleys, glacial rivers, and panoramic mountain vistas create a landscape that inspires both exploration and reflection. Serving as the gateway to destinations such as Gangotri, Gaumukh, and Dayara Bugyal, the town attracts pilgrims, trekkers, mountaineers, and nature enthusiasts alike.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Whether watching the Bhagirathi flow through the valley, admiring the changing colours of the Himalayan peaks, or embarking on a mountain adventure, visitors discover experiences that are both exhilarating and deeply peaceful.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "March to June offers pleasant weather, clear skies, and ideal conditions for sightseeing, trekking, and outdoor activities. The post-monsoon season from September to November is equally rewarding, with crisp mountain views and comfortable temperatures. Winter, from December to February , transforms the surrounding higher reaches into a snowy wonderland, attracting visitors seeking a classic Himalayan experience.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "By Air: The nearest airport is Jolly Grant Airport, Dehradun (DED) , located approximately 165 km from Uttarkashi. Taxis and regular transport services are available from the airport.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "By Train: The nearest major railway station is Dehradun Railway Station , about 145 km away, with good connectivity to Delhi and other major Indian cities.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "By Road: Uttarkashi is well connected by road to Dehradun, Rishikesh, Haridwar , and Mussoorie . Regular state-run and private buses, along with taxis, operate on these routes, making road travel convenient and scenic.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Uttarkashi",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/uttarakhand/uttarkashi",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:50.898644+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
